; Leg HC -- flow-control CONTROL leg (--noflow).  Host SENDS.
;
; BENCH take-file: there is no "set line" here.  ~/.kermrc names the adapter.
; CHECK THAT IT NAMES THE ONE THAT IS PLUGGED IN.
;
; Run HD IMMEDIATELY after this.  Adjacent pairs only: the same CKPRE binary
; gave 18.29 s non-line in SS16ah and 21.43 s in SS16al with the wire held
; constant.  The spread is the HOST.
;
; PRECONDITION, AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL (SS16am):
;     kermit -C "show versions, exit"                    -> 11.0.508
;     kermit -C "show features, exit" | grep -i crtscts  -> POSIX_CRTSCTS
;     stty -f <port> crtscts -hupcl                      -> and read it back
; CK_RTSCTS alone only makes the COMMAND legal.  If the client here is still
; 9.0.302, STOP AND REBUILD IT -- running the pair without POSIX_CRTSCTS
; reproduces SS16al leg GB, which looked like a clean positive result and was
; retracted one section later.
;
; READ IT WITH:
;     python3 v9k/tools/pktstat.py --rxbytes <from STEPHC.OUT> s16bcHC.pkt
; Residual -11 clean, +28 with a startup timeout.
; cmp FIRST, then the counters.  A leg that is fast and wrong is the failure.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
set retry 30
log packets s16bcHC.pkt
send rcvhc.dat
statistics
